AgX was created by Troy Sobotka. These LUTs use Eary Chow's version of AgX:
https://github.com/EaryChow/AgX

The LUTs come from Blender 4.5's bundled colour-management configuration
(datafiles/colormanagement) and are distributed under the GNU General Public
License (GNU GPL).

web/tools/agx_lut.py converts luminance_compensation_bt2020.cube (37^3) and
AgX_Base_sRGB.cube (57^3) to agx_lut.bin.gz: RGB, red fastest, rounded to
16-bit values at a scale of 64000, delta-coded along red modulo 65536,
stored little-endian, then gzip-compressed. The cubes retain their bundled
order: luminance compensation first, AgX base second.
